{"author":{"id":"8d2e0405f08ac6c481f912544d6d5c0f58b2dc14a7e51ad4d499ee7a34567943"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794302007,"nonce":"kqp3TtXdY9/aij931H0Q+K9OlG4=","title":"Periodic N1E re-mesh replaces a structured lattice with a gmsh mesh","message":"Domain._remesh_periodic re-meshes any shape-backed domain with gmsh setPeriodic when jno.fem sees periodic ties on an N1E field. For a .structured() plan this silently swaps the lattice for a free mesh, although the lattice already matches node for node across opposite faces.\n\nReproduce: jno.shape.box(0,0,0,1,1,1,size=0.25).structured().domain(), N1E curl-curl + mass with ties face('left')-face('right'); the point count changes after jno.fem.","files":null}]}